Chapter: F69Warns

 A program that compiles cleanly and produces exactly one WARNING, to prove
 codexzig now reports what it used to discard.

 `is-digit` is a builtin. Defining one shadows it, which is CDX3005 -- a
 warning, not an error, so the halt gate does not fire and the old harness
 said nothing at all. That is the whole point of the probe: it must build,
 and it must still tell you something.

 We say:

Section: Shadow

  is-digit : Char -> Boolean
  is-digit (c) = char-code c == 3

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (if is-digit (char-at "0" 0) then "zero is a digit" else "no")
  end
